{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-15T09:19:49.138Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"489731d8ab76ae02b28618d0","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_edit","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/comments/2/text","value":"Review rounds on PR #1734 settled two things about the shared clock that this item's health and context counts use:\n\n- **The clock.** It is the newer of `updated_at` and the latest history entry. Round 1 briefly narrowed it to `updated_at` alone, but Greptile then showed that `pm restore` writes the historical document with its older `updated_at` and appends a new entry, so the stream has to count. The printed `--updated-before` sweeps are therefore candidate lists by metadata time: an item restored inside the window can appear in a sweep without being in the advisory count, and `--takeover-stale` re-judges each item under the lock.\n- **Quoting.** Custom status ids are shell-quoted in every remedy.\n\nDetails are on pm-gh1336."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2/edited_at","value":"2026-11-15T09:19:49.137Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-15T09:19:49.138Z"}],"before_hash":"611214f37cf29e6f2ef0769975314e0751eb1738e17931d4ef043dca1b34d36e","after_hash":"ef42971f8a0ea4cf01306780d1f0cb699f0be5ac3fa9e2c901b23fb1ce96e672","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"313166952e2f4646990fcc1a15cf02763a6648d88e38c57606b5089fe9f7759d"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-15T09:46:23.928Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"489731d8ab76ae02b28618d0","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-15T09:46:23.928Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review round 3 on PR #1734: details.in_progress_work.item_remedies gains take_over_idle (pm claim <id> --takeover-stale) for idle items another agent holds, because a plain pm claim refuses them. The idle clock now ignores maintenance-only history entries such as history-compact, so compaction cannot hide abandoned work."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-15T09:46:23.928Z"}],"before_hash":"ef42971f8a0ea4cf01306780d1f0cb699f0be5ac3fa9e2c901b23fb1ce96e672","after_hash":"020f748f501962ca862268fc1d4e9851fd2f090fc386819e470bd499945a8dd8","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"2937409eccadfbd28a76e80c139dfab94372a1082e0f94322fd75b74e48e9d29"}
